				<path class="fig-pen" d="M412 240 L418 248 L426 241" />

				<text class="fig-pen-text" x="48" y="298">
					Holds within these bounds, and no further.
				</text>

				<rect class="fig-bar" x="48" y="318" width="384" height="6" />
				<rect class="fig-bar" x="48" y="332" width="350" height="6" />
				<rect class="fig-bar" x="48" y="346" width="370" height="6" />
			</svg>
			<figcaption>
				Figure 1. The front page of every opinion. The reliance statement bounds
				it to the decision reviewed, the material examined and the date it was
				issued.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>

		<h2 id="how-it-runs">How it runs</h2>
		<p>
			Scope and end date are agreed before work starts, and a review
			typically takes 3 to 4 weeks from kickoff. The fee is fixed,
			proposed after a first call, and it does not change once agreed. There
			is no time-and-materials billing.
		</p>

		<h2 id="independence">The independence rule</h2>
		<p>
			On any review I take no delivery work and no supplier-side work, and I
			have no stake in the outcome. Any interest is declared before the
			engagement starts, and if a conflict cannot be cleanly separated I
			decline the engagement.
		</p>

		<h2 id="out-of-scope">Out of scope</h2>
		<p>
			The review does not include implementation or delivery resource, and it
			does not run a supplier selection, though a completed selection can be
			reviewed. It carries no certification and no regulatory sign-off. The
			supplier's technical work is examined but not redone.
		</p>

		<h2 id="questions">Common questions</h2>
		{
			questions.map(({ q, a }) => (
				<Fragment>
					<h3>{q}</h3>
					<p>{a}</p>
				</Fragment>
			))
		}

		<h2 id="beyond-the-review">Beyond the review</h2>
		<p>
			Some owners keep me on as an adviser after a review, and the other ways
			to engage are described under <a href="/work/">Work</a>. If a review is
			not the shape of what you need, say so in the same message.
		</p>

		<h2 id="start-here">Start here</h2>
		<p>
			<a href="/contact/">Tell me the decision you are facing</a> and when
			it has to be made.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>
